  "purpose": "route B v8 keeps the single-arbiter planner and the v7 recovery harness exactly as declared and replaces only the recovery bearing, because the offline replay of v7 over the recorded blind runs showed the pure retrace is nearly inert in the measured geometry: the terminal losses happen while the hero holds its final approach, so the last two known positions differ by about 0.02 px and there is nothing to reverse. v8 therefore declares bounded_retrace_or_waypoint: retrace whenever the reversed last-known displacement is usable and region-safe, and otherwise re-aim at the current waypoint, still region-checked at the current retreat depth and still capped by maximum_recovery_steps. The localization-gap guard still ends the episode CAPTURE_FAILURE/localization_gap, so a failed recovery is never a silent success, and an unanchored episode still waits rather than guessing.",
